1
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:08,725
Day thirty-one.

2
00:00:08,965 --> 00:00:10,395
Our plant is drooping.

3
00:00:10,615 --> 00:00:13,125
Last time, Momo asked: is it sad?

4
00:00:13,181 --> 00:00:13,881
Well?

5
00:00:14,051 --> 00:00:14,921
Is it?

6
00:00:15,236 --> 00:00:16,946
A drooping plant isn't sad.

7
00:00:17,176 --> 00:00:18,356
It needs something.

8
00:00:18,566 --> 00:00:20,066
Did you lock in your answer?

9
00:00:20,296 --> 00:00:21,476
Hold on to it.

10
00:00:21,987 --> 00:00:24,797
So the Buddies built a hotel on our window ledge.

11
00:00:25,027 --> 00:00:26,017
Three rooms.

12
00:00:26,257 --> 00:00:27,317
Three guests.

13
00:00:27,547 --> 00:00:29,947
Every guest must get everything it needs.

14
00:00:30,167 --> 00:00:31,267
By sunset.

15
00:00:31,402 --> 00:00:34,752
Three guests: our plant, our mealworm, and a mystery guest.

16
00:00:35,184 --> 00:00:36,744
It's You against the Buddies.

17
00:00:36,964 --> 00:00:38,244
You lock in first.

18
00:00:38,454 --> 00:00:41,354
Every time you are right, put up one finger on your other

19
00:00:41,104 --> 00:00:41,794
hand.

20
00:00:42,014 --> 00:00:43,744
No lock-in, no point.

21
00:00:43,964 --> 00:00:46,174
And a lizard is hiding in this video.

22
00:00:46,413 --> 00:00:47,234
Find it!

23
00:00:47,674 --> 00:00:51,584
Today you will learn what a drooping plant needs, why living things

24
00:00:51,334 --> 00:00:54,194
need water, and why living things need air.

25
00:00:54,465 --> 00:00:55,385
Are you ready?

26
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:56,565
Three!

27
00:00:56,955 --> 00:00:57,595
Two!

28
00:00:57,965 --> 00:00:58,595
One!

29
00:00:58,995 --> 00:00:59,665
Go!

30
00:01:01,048 --> 00:01:01,928
Round one.

31
00:01:02,188 --> 00:01:03,058
Room one.

32
00:01:03,278 --> 00:01:04,728
The plant is drooping.

33
00:01:04,968 --> 00:01:05,958
What does it need?

34
00:01:06,258 --> 00:01:07,238
One, water.

35
00:01:07,468 --> 00:01:08,368
Two, food.

36
00:01:08,618 --> 00:01:09,618
Three, air.

37
00:01:09,848 --> 00:01:11,258
Show me with your fingers.

38
00:01:16,728 --> 00:01:17,678
Locked in!

39
00:01:17,808 --> 00:01:18,758
Two, food!

40
00:01:18,838 --> 00:01:19,819
It's hungry.

41
00:01:19,849 --> 00:01:21,099
Give it my biscuit!

42
00:01:21,149 --> 00:01:21,929
One, water.

43
00:01:21,679 --> 00:01:23,889
I touched the soil.

44
00:01:24,149 --> 00:01:25,329
It is dry.

45
00:01:25,378 --> 00:01:26,358
One, water.

46
00:01:26,558 --> 00:01:28,298
Nobody watered it yesterday.

47
00:01:28,408 --> 00:01:29,668
But is it sad?

48
00:01:30,014 --> 00:01:31,594
Let's test Pip's idea.

49
00:01:31,804 --> 00:01:33,164
Pip waters the soil.

50
00:01:33,404 --> 00:01:34,404
Now we wait.

51
00:01:34,624 --> 00:01:36,154
This takes a few hours.

52
00:01:36,374 --> 00:01:38,684
So let's shrink down and follow the water.

53
00:01:38,884 --> 00:01:39,764
Quietly.

54
00:01:42,989 --> 00:01:44,219
You are tiny now.

55
00:01:44,489 --> 00:01:46,859
You are in the wet soil, with the water.

56
00:01:47,745 --> 00:01:48,945
In through a root.

57
00:01:50,855 --> 00:01:51,895
Up the stem.

58
00:01:53,810 --> 00:01:55,210
All the way to a leaf.

59
00:01:57,123 --> 00:01:59,063
Plants need water to make food.

60
00:02:01,369 --> 00:02:02,629
A few hours later.

61
00:02:02,869 --> 00:02:03,499
Look!

62
00:02:03,739 --> 00:02:05,579
The plant is standing up again.

63
00:02:05,789 --> 00:02:07,069
The answer is one.

64
00:02:07,319 --> 00:02:08,059
Water.

65
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:12,030
Say it with me!

66
00:02:12,737 --> 00:02:13,867
It is wilting.

67
00:02:14,117 --> 00:02:15,827
It does not have enough water.

68
00:02:19,974 --> 00:02:21,703
That is what the drooping was.

69
00:02:21,913 --> 00:02:23,453
The plant is not sad.

70
00:02:23,684 --> 00:02:24,834
It was wilting.

71
00:02:24,885 --> 00:02:25,855
Not sad.

72
00:02:25,965 --> 00:02:26,975
Wilting!

73
00:02:27,476 --> 00:02:28,675
Showed one finger?

74
00:02:28,925 --> 00:02:30,796
One finger up on your score hand!

75
00:02:30,996 --> 00:02:32,286
More biscuit for me.

76
00:02:32,786 --> 00:02:36,246
All living things such as plants and animals need water.

77
00:02:36,367 --> 00:02:37,267
The plant.

78
00:02:37,477 --> 00:02:39,647
The mealworm, with its juicy carrot.

79
00:02:39,867 --> 00:02:40,747
And you!

80
00:02:41,249 --> 00:02:43,159
We need water to digest food.

81
00:02:43,379 --> 00:02:46,239
We need water to carry out our daily activities.

82
00:02:46,449 --> 00:02:49,209
We need water to remove waste from our body.

83
00:02:51,111 --> 00:02:53,361
Room two is ready for our mealworm.

84
00:02:53,561 --> 00:02:55,281
A jar with a tight lid.

85
00:02:55,451 --> 00:02:56,721
Safe and snug!

86
00:02:57,142 --> 00:02:59,172
Something is not right with this room.

87
00:02:59,392 --> 00:03:01,492
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

88
00:03:01,722 --> 00:03:02,622
Hold on!

89
00:03:08,129 --> 00:03:09,239
Arms crossed?

90
00:03:09,459 --> 00:03:10,599
One finger up!

91
00:03:10,819 --> 00:03:11,489
Look.

92
00:03:11,749 --> 00:03:13,209
The lid is shut tight.

93
00:03:13,439 --> 00:03:14,659
Air cannot get in.

94
00:03:14,713 --> 00:03:16,813
Our glass box has holes in its lid!

95
00:03:16,864 --> 00:03:17,764
Holes!

96
00:03:17,975 --> 00:03:19,044
I forgot.

97
00:03:19,214 --> 00:03:20,704
Sorry, little guest.

98
00:03:21,278 --> 00:03:23,738
A new lid, with holes, so air can get in.

99
00:03:24,703 --> 00:03:25,813
Say it with me!

100
00:03:26,524 --> 00:03:29,644
Living things breathe in air that contains oxygen.

101
00:03:34,329 --> 00:03:35,899
Now our guest can move in.

102
00:03:36,139 --> 00:03:37,419
Air, through the holes.

103
00:03:37,669 --> 00:03:38,809
Oats, for food.

104
00:03:39,059 --> 00:03:40,849
A juicy carrot, for water.

105
00:03:41,496 --> 00:03:43,486
All living things need air to live.

106
00:03:43,612 --> 00:03:45,102
Even plants need air.

107
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:46,620
One guest.

108
00:03:46,850 --> 00:03:47,910
Three needs.

109
00:03:48,281 --> 00:03:49,341
Say it with us!

110
00:03:50,001 --> 00:03:50,691
Water!

111
00:03:50,413 --> 00:03:51,104
Food!

112
00:03:50,826 --> 00:03:51,516
Air!

113
00:03:53,301 --> 00:03:55,051
Living things need all three!

114
00:03:56,601 --> 00:03:57,291
Water!

115
00:03:57,013 --> 00:03:57,703
Food!

116
00:03:57,426 --> 00:03:58,116
Air!

117
00:03:58,251 --> 00:04:00,001
Living things need all three!

118
00:04:00,856 --> 00:04:02,246
Show me your score hand!

119
00:04:02,466 --> 00:04:03,466
Two fingers?

120
00:04:03,676 --> 00:04:04,956
You beat the Buddies.

121
00:04:05,176 --> 00:04:06,176
High five!

122
00:04:06,822 --> 00:04:08,182
Did you spot the lizard?

123
00:04:08,432 --> 00:04:10,952
It was on the wall, above the hotel sign.

124
00:04:11,162 --> 00:04:12,712
Does a lizard need water?

125
00:04:12,952 --> 00:04:14,222
Tell someone at home.

126
00:04:14,875 --> 00:04:17,035
Let's read today's key words together!

127
00:04:17,275 --> 00:04:17,995
Ready?

128
00:04:18,285 --> 00:04:18,995
Water.

129
00:04:20,401 --> 00:04:21,261
Wilting.

130
00:04:22,772 --> 00:04:23,692
Oxygen.

131
00:04:25,269 --> 00:04:26,169
Well done!

132
00:04:26,967 --> 00:04:27,967
Five ticks.

133
00:04:28,207 --> 00:04:29,177
Four to go.

134
00:04:29,307 --> 00:04:30,797
The mealworm has oats.

135
00:04:30,827 --> 00:04:32,557
But nobody feeds a plant.

136
00:04:32,597 --> 00:04:34,157
So who feeds a plant?

137
00:04:34,731 --> 00:04:35,691
Room three.

138
00:04:35,911 --> 00:04:38,041
A bean plant from Pip's dark cupboard.

139
00:04:38,261 --> 00:04:39,811
It had water every day.

140
00:04:40,051 --> 00:04:40,951
It had air.

141
00:04:41,151 --> 00:04:43,231
But something is wrong under this cloth.

142
00:04:43,451 --> 00:04:44,671
What is it missing?

143
00:04:44,911 --> 00:04:46,391
Find out in Part Two!

144
00:04:47,526 --> 00:04:48,587
Say it with us!

145
00:04:49,387 --> 00:04:50,097
Ready?

146
00:04:50,222 --> 00:04:50,842
One!

147
00:04:51,222 --> 00:04:51,902
Two!

148
00:04:52,227 --> 00:04:53,402
Now you know!
